From 0742ec2fd79d6ab540d853b66608fa1fb2b70451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rieki777 <rieki@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 17:05:09 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(quality): final audit pass on path-progression UI
 (security + empty state + a11y)

Four quality improvements from a final audit across everything we
shipped today:

1. Security: markBonusClaimed is now adminProcedure (was
   protectedProcedure with self-targeting). The normal flow runs
   through the Hypha Alchemy webhook in webhook-receiver.ts which
   flips the flags on on-chain confirmation. Letting any user
   self-flip the flag was a small audit-accuracy hole; restricting to
   admin closes it without breaking the auto-flip path. Procedure now
   takes a userId so admins can target other users for manual
   reconciliation.

2. Empty state: when the path filter narrows EpicQuestSection's pool
   to zero (e.g. a player picks Investor and we have no water-element
   Epic quests yet), render a calm 'No water-themed Epic Quests yet,
   the forest grows season by season' message with a 'See all Epic
   Quests' link that clears the filter via window.location, instead
   of an empty carousel.

3. Scroll anchors: the citizenship tier pills (Co-Creator pill in the
   horizontal sidebar) now scroll to id='rites-of-passage' which is
   added to the 'Rites & Quests by Season' section in Quest.tsx.
   Steward and Sage pills point at the existing id='epic-quests'
   section. Explorer falls back to scroll-to-top because Welcome
   Aboard lives on /profile, not /quest.

4. Accessibility: canopy-fall keyframe now respects
   prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, falling back to opacity:1 +
   transform:none + filter:none. Reduced-motion users see the new
   Open Universe reveals appear without the drift animation.

Also a tiny copy cleanup: replaced one stray em-dash in a Quest.tsx
build comment with a colon.

No schema changes. Pure code-quality improvements on the same
user-facing surface.

